  "//": "First-pass config for the PUF secure-boot demo, adapted from top_pd/config_mixed_3.json's 'mixed' strategy (ibex_core+ibex_top, uart, xbar_tlul_2to5 synthesized directly from RTL; only the three real SRAMs -- 21-bank IMEM, 1KiB ESRAM/DMEM, and the PUF's own foundry SRAM primitive -- are hard macros). DIE_AREA (6500x4500 = 29.25mm^2) is a generous first guess: the 21-bank IMEM macro alone is 5000x2500um (12.5mm^2, dominates the floorplan), plus ~0.956mm^2 for ESRAM+DMEM, ~0.10mm^2 for the PUF SRAM, and roughly 1.7mm^2 of synthesized std-cell logic (ibex/uart/xbar/glue) -- about 14.9mm^2 of raw component area, so this budgets close to 2x margin for routing/PDN. Like config_mixed_3's own note when it went from hard-macro to synthesized ibex/uart/xbar, expect to iterate (shrink die and/or adjust density) once real placement/routing results come back. u_puf_regif.u_puf.u_sram's exact post-synthesis instance path should be double-checked against Yosys's actual hierarchy naming on the first run -- flattening behavior can rename nested paths."
